 10. **The owner keeps its model binding:** `class Web4MDA extends UcpComponent<Web4MDAModel>` — no inlining, no `implements` of the model.
 11. **`ItemView` is NOT a model** (Tron, 2026-10-03: *"ItemView is a unit class of UcpComponent that implements View. a layer 5 implementation. skip it for now. we will implement MVC in one of the next plans."*). `ItemModel` stays `ItemModel` and stays separate from `Displayable`.
 12. **A role-less `containedBy` is a header clause on interfaces too** (oopPO 2026-10-03, extending ruling F4 from classes to interfaces; flagged to Tron): `interface FileServerModel extends ItemModel containedBy DefaultFolder`. Ownership stays a RELATIONSHIP UNIT as Tron ruled for the file units (plan 2026-10-01 MA3: each moved class's model carries exactly one `containedBy` to its owner) — never deleted, never derived. *Corrected 2026-10-03: oopPO had first ruled the model's `containedBy` a duplicate to delete with a derived placement rule; that would have overturned the ratified MA3.*
+13. **`packagedIn X` — a sub-component lives in the component X, which is thereby a Package** (Tron, 2026-10-05, plan mode: *"Ior is a UcpComponent … it becomes a Package when it contains UcpComponents next to its own version. Automatically and always."* — and, asked how the model records it: a NEW relationship kind **`packagedIn`**, a relationship UNIT). A header clause on classes and interfaces, at most one: `class RepositoryId extends UcpComponent<RepositoryIdModel> packagedIn Ior`. `ClassModel.namespace` is **DERIVED** from it (the container's namespace + the container's name) — ONE fact; a stored namespace beside a `packagedIn` is an error. Distinct from a role-less `containedBy`, which makes a UNIT (no own folder): a `packagedIn` component keeps its own folder, beside the container's own `latest` ([eamd-ucp.md](eamd-ucp.md) rule 6).
+14. **A `dependency` is a COLLECTION and a BIDIRECTIONAL relationship** (Tron, 2026-10-05: *"a Thinglish dependency is a Thinglish collection. it should be bidirectional navigatable and therefore it needs to be modeled as a bidirectional relationship in the MDA M3,M2 tree"*): the dependency end (what a class depends on) is the one stored fact (its imports); the opposite end — its **dependants** — is DERIVED, never stored ([mof.md](mof.md): `M3Relationship.opposite`, `M2AbstractDependency extends M2AbstractCollection`). `move()` uses the dependants end to adjust every dependant.
 
